    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the \"reject future `registrationDate`\" rule for `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate.java` \u2014 a guard step that reads the published `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` and throws `FutureRegistrationDateException` when `registrationDate` is present and strictly after `LocalDate.now()`. An absent date passes through (it defaults to the server date later in `BuildOwner`).\n- `rest/function/owner/FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 a checked exception so it's routed to its escalation handler.\n- `rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with the same `OwnerFieldErrors` `errors`-array contract used by the other create-time field validators, naming `registrationDate`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- Inserted a `validateRegistrationDate` step into `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` between `validatePostcode` and `normalize`, so validation happens before the owner is built/persisted.\n\nThe rule treats a date *equal* to today as valid and only rejects dates strictly later than the server date, matching \"later than the server date.\" `src/test/java/.../AcceptanceTest.java::errorRejectsFutureDate` (payload with `registrationDate: 2999-01-01`) now returns 400, and the full suite passes.",
